                "headline": "Flood Watch issued November 9 at 9:36PM PST until November 11 at 10:00PM PST by NWS Seattle WA",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of northwest Washington, including the following\ncounty, Mason.\n\n* WHEN...From Tuesday evening through Wednesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Two to three and half inches of rain is forecast for the south\nslopes of the Olympics Tuesday into Wednesday morning. Snow\nlevels will be between 8000 and 9500 feet. The combination of\nheavy rain with high snow levels could push the Skokomish River\nnear Potlatch above flood stage.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
